% SECTION IV: PROPOSED METHOD
% =========================================
\section{Proposed Future-Aware PPO Agent}
\label{sec:method}

In this section, we present the architecture of our Lyapunov-Inspired Future-Aware PPO agent. The system comprises three key modules: (1) The Future-Aware State Space construction, (2) The Neural Network Architecture (Actor-Critic), and (3) The Lyapunov-Regularized Reward Mechanism.

\subsection{Future-Aware State Space}
The state $s_t$ observed by the agent at decision step $t$ is formulated to encompass both historical network context and future video dynamics:
\begin{equation}
    s_t = \big( \vec{x}_t, b_t, a_{t-1}, \vec{v}_{t:t+M-1}, \vec{c}_{t:t+M-1} \big)
\end{equation}
where $\vec{x}_t$ represents the vector of past throughput measurements, $b_t$ is the current buffer occupancy, and $a_{t-1}$ is the previously selected bitrate level. Crucially, to empower the future-aware mechanism, we augment the state with $\vec{v}_{t:t+M-1}$, which contains the sizes and expected VMAF scores of the upcoming $M$ chunks, and $\vec{c}_{t:t+M-1}$, encompassing the Spatial Information (SI) and Temporal Information (TI) of those future scenes. This explicit inclusion of $M$-step lookahead data is what distinguishes our state space from traditional reactive agents.

\subsection{Network Architecture}
We employ an Actor-Critic architecture based on PPO. 
The input features are processed through two separate branches:
\begin{itemize}
    \item 1D-CNN Branch: The historical throughput vector ($\vec{x}_t$) is passed through a 1D Convolutional Neural Network (128 filters, kernel size 4) to extract temporal network patterns.
    \item MLP (Multi-Layer Perceptron) Branch: The remaining scalar/vector inputs ($b_t, a_{t-1}, \vec{v}_{t:t+M-1}, \vec{c}_{t:t+M-1}$) are processed via fully connected layers to capture content-aware and future-aware context.
\end{itemize}
The outputs of these branches are concatenated and fed into the shared hidden layers (two layers of 128 units with Tanh activation). Finally, the network splits into:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Actor Head: Outputs a probability distribution $\pi(a|s)$ over the discrete bitrate actions using a Softmax layer.
    \item Critic Head: Outputs the estimated value function $V(s)$ used to compute the advantage function.
\end{enumerate}

