\subsection{Lyapunov-Regularized PPO Training}
Standard PPO optimizes a clipped surrogate objective function. We modify this objective by integrating the Lyapunov drift. The reward function $r_t$ is dynamically adjusted based on the ``virtual queue'' drift derived in Section III:
\begin{equation}
    r_t^{Lya} = \underbrace{QoE_t}_{\text{Performance}} - \underbrace{\beta \cdot \max(0, B_{ref} - B_t)}_{\text{Stability Constraint}}
\end{equation}
If the buffer $B_t$ is safely above $B_{ref}$, the penalty term vanishes, and the agent behaves like a standard QoE maximizer. However, as $B_t$ drops below $B_{ref}$, the penalty grows linearly, forcing the agent to prioritize buffer replenishment over high bitrate. 
The detailed training procedure is summarized in Algorithm 1.

% --- Algorithm Pseudocode ---
\begin{algorithm*}[t]
\caption{Lyapunov-Inspired Future-Aware PPO Training}
\label{alg:training}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\STATE Initialize: Actor $\pi_\theta$, Critic $V_\phi$, Buffer $B_0=0$
\STATE Parameters: $\beta$ (Penalty coef), $B_{ref}$ (Safe buffer), $\gamma$ (Discount), $H$ (Steps per episode)
\FOR{episode $= 1$ to $MaxEpisodes$}
    \STATE Reset environment, observe state $s_0$
    \FOR{step $t = 0$ to $H$}
        \STATE Agent selects bitrate $a_t \sim \pi_\theta(a_t|s_t)$
        \STATE Download chunk, observe new state $s_{t+1}$
        \STATE Calculate standard reward $r_t^{QoE}$ (Eq. 4)
        \STATE Calculate Lyapunov Penalty: $P_t = \beta \cdot \max(0, B_{ref} - B_t)$
        \STATE Final Reward: $r_t \leftarrow r_t^{QoE} - P_t$
        \STATE Store transition $(s_t, a_t, r_t, s_{t+1})$ in memory
        \IF{Update Interval}
            \STATE Compute advantages $A_t$ using GAE
            \STATE Update $\theta$ via PPO Clipping Objective
            \STATE Update $\phi$ to minimize MSE of Value loss
        \ENDIF
    \ENDFOR
\ENDFOR
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm*}

