\section{Experimental Evaluation}
\label{sec:eval}

In this section, we provide a comprehensive evaluation of the proposed Lyapunov-Inspired Future-Aware PPO agent. We aim to answer three key research questions:
\begin{itemize}
    \item RQ1 (Tail-Risk and Overall Performance): Can a stability-guided RL agent achieve highly competitive QoE while significantly suppressing catastrophic stall risks compared to aggressive optimization baselines?
    \item RQ2 (Stability \& Safety): Can the Lyapunov constraint effectively reduce catastrophic rebuffering events and bitrate oscillations compared to pure RL and control-theoretic methods?
    \item RQ3 (Component Efficacy): What is the individual contribution of ``Future Awareness'' and ``Lyapunov Shaping'' to the final performance?
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Experimental Setup}
\label{subsec:exp_setup}

Datasets and Network Traces: We evaluate our proposed method using real-world network traces from diverse environments. Our standard training and evaluation rely on a combination of broadband traces provided by the FCC Measuring Broadband America program \cite{fcc2015mba} and 3G/HSDPA mobile datasets from the Norway Nornet Edge platform \cite{kvalbein2014}. To rigorously test the zero-shot generalization and robustness of our agent, we additionally employ a highly volatile 5G mmWave dataset \cite{meng2024mmwave}. Unlike traditional networks, the 5G mmWave traces exhibit extreme bandwidth fluctuations, swinging from multi-gigabit capacities to near-zero throughput (starvation) during sudden physical blockages.

Baselines: We benchmark our Proposed agent against the following state-of-the-art ABR algorithms:
\begin{itemize}
    \item RobustMPC \cite{yin2015control}: A leading control-theoretic approach that uses harmonic throughput predictions to solve a receding horizon optimization problem.
    \item Pensieve \cite{mao2017neural}: A prominent pure Deep Reinforcement Learning agent trained without explicit control heuristics or future chunk awareness.
    \item BBA \cite{huang2014buffer}: A classic heuristic method that maps the current buffer occupancy directly to the available bitrate levels.
    \item Fugu \cite{yan2020learning}: A supervised/imitation learning approach trained to mimic an optimal MPC oracle using deep neural networks.
    \item \textbf{Genie (Oracle):} An offline baseline that possesses perfect, non-causal knowledge of the entire future network trace \cite{mao2017neural}. Rather than serving as a strict mathematical upper bound for our specific empirical QoE formulation, it operates as a powerful structural benchmark that leverages perfect future knowledge to prioritize near-zero rebuffering over aggressive VMAF maximization.
\end{itemize}

